			"date": "2024-08-09T13:43:11.532Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.online/@stvfrnzl\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>stvfrnzl</span></a></span> what’s EmpathyLab?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112932538789943363",
			"parentId": "112932355540994656",
			"url": "https://mastodon.online/@stvfrnzl/112932538719935700",
			"author": {
				"name": "Steve Frenzel",
				"url": "https://mastodon.online/@stvfrnzl",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/510/974/973/019/589/original/2f10c129f9b865b1.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-08-09T14:29:46.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> it's a place where people can experience different kinds of disabilities while using (a website) or interacting with something </p><p>They would wear glasses simulating certain visual impairments, such as cataracts or tunnel vision and are given tasks, like solving a maze or puzzle</p><p>Or use browser extensions simulating Parkinson's while booking tickets </p><p>It's a great way to introduce people to the topic of accessibility and can make it easier to relate</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112932646468750912",
			"parentId": "112932538789943363",
