				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/510/974/973/019/589/original/2f10c129f9b865b1.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-08-09T15:05:39.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> not that I'm aware of, but I think big companies like Apple and Google have these, someone might have written about it</p><p>I recently participated in a workshop part of a tech festival in Germany where they had one and I will do the same at my work place</p><p>In my experience showing assistive technology and accessibility issues in real life had the biggest impact to change people's perspective on it</p><p>Way more than showing slides or videos or blog posts 🤗</p>",
